      "body": "# [Bugfix][collect-env] Distinguish CUDA Toolkit and Runtime versions\n\n## Before\n\n`vllm collect-env` used `nvcc --version` for the field named `CUDA runtime\nversion`:\n\n```text\nCUDA runtime version : 13.3.73\n```\n\nThis value was actually the CUDA Toolkit version. The output did not identify\nthe CUDA Runtime loaded by the process, and the two versions can differ.\n\n## After\n\nThe output distinguishes the two sources:\n\n```text\nCUDA Toolkit version : 13.3.73\nCUDA Runtime version : 13.0\n```\n\n`CUDA Toolkit version` continues to come from `nvcc --version`. The new\n`CUDA Runtime version` is obtained through `cudaRuntimeGetVersion()`, with\nfallbacks for CUDA libraries in `CUDA_HOME`/`CUDA_PATH`, NVIDIA CUDA Python\nwheels, and the system linker path. The lookup targets Linux/WSL, which is\nvLLM's supported CUDA platform; native Windows support is outside the scope of\nthis change. The cuDNN field is unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Installed the current worktree into the existing venv with\n  `VLLM_USE_PRECOMPILED=1 uv pip install -e . --torch-backend=auto`.\n- Ran `vllm collect-env` successfully.\n- Verified the output:\n\n  ```text\n  Is CUDA available            : True\n  CUDA Toolkit version         : 13.3.73\n  CUDA Runtime version         : 13.0\n  ```\n\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- No model evaluation is needed; this changes diagnostics only.\n\nNo open PR was found addressing this CUDA Toolkit/Runtime reporting issue.\nExisting `collect-env` work is focused on ROCm reporting or other unrelated\ndiagnostics.\n\nAI assistance was used for this change.\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "Alex-ai-future"
            },
            "body": "Hi @hmellor @DarkLight1337, would you mind taking a look at this focused `collect-env` fix when you have time?\n\nIt distinguishes the CUDA Toolkit version reported by `nvcc` from the CUDA Runtime version reported by `cudaRuntimeGetVersion()`. I’d especially appreciate your feedback on the runtime library lookup and the scope of the change.\n\nThanks!\n",
